        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Landau and Lifshitz, The Classical Theory of Fields, 4th revised English edition",
              "url": "https://ru.djvu.online/file/ADnW1S0k8Ttos",
              "locator": "Complete text inspected; §75, printed pp. 222–225, on the nonrelativistic radiation-reaction equation and its future-boundary solution."
            },
            {
              "title": "Sen Zhang, Pre-acceleration from Landau–Lifshitz Series, arXiv:1303.7120",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/1303.7120",
              "locator": "Full HTML text inspected; §2, Eqs. (2.1)–(2.6), and Appendix A, Eqs. (A.1)–(A.4), including the nonrelativistic pre-acceleration solution."
            }
          ]
        },
        "dependency_level": 0,
        "physical_scope": "Exact solution and sign check for a separately stated one-dimensional nonrelativistic Abraham–Lorentz ODE. Pre-acceleration is a property of this future-boundary model solution, not an empirical finding or a conclusion about finite-body causal dynamics."
      },
      {
        "id": "cex-rpm-lad-force-free-runaway",
        "kind": "counterexample",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Force-free runaway solution of the LAD equation",
        "statement": "Assume the flat effective LAD postulate [[post-rpm-lad-effective-equation]] with $\\tau_e>0$ and take $F\\equiv0$. In Minkowski coordinates $(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3)$, choose constants $\\theta_0\\in\\mathbb R$, $A\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{0\\}$ with units $\\mathrm{s}^{-1}$, and $\\tau_0\\in\\mathbb R$. Define for all $\\tau\\in\\mathbb R$\n\n$$\n\\theta(\\tau):=\\theta_0+A\\tau_e e^{(\\tau-\\tau_0)/\\tau_e},\\qquad\nU(\\tau):=c(\\cosh\\theta(\\tau),\\sinh\\theta(\\tau),0,0),\n$$\n\nand let $x(\\tau)=x_0+\\int_{\\tau_0}^{\\tau}U(s)\\,ds$. Then $x$ is a smooth future-timelike worldline parametrized by proper time, and it solves the adopted LAD equation with zero external force. Its proper acceleration magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{\\eta(a,a)}=c|A|e^{(\\tau-\\tau_0)/\\tau_e},\n$$\n\nso it grows exponentially as $\\tau\\to+\\infty$. By contrast, the force-free reduced LL field in [[lem-rpm-ll-reduced-ode]] is zero on the shell and has constant-velocity solutions. This is a counterexample about the adopted ODEs, not an observed phenomenon or a statement about finite-body electrodynamics.",
        "deps": [
          "post-rpm-lad-effective-equation",
          "def-rpm-charge-spin-model",
          "lem-rpm-ll-reduced-ode",
          "def-hyperbolic-functions",
          "thm-hyperbolic-identities-and-derivatives",
          "thm-derivative-of-exponential",
          "thm-chain-rule",
